@tradition twelve-weeks-aboard
// Twelve weeks aboard (0.92.6 item 7 (c), FX17; lead 35's yes): Day 84 after you came aboard, a Sunday. A toast at the
// Sunday table in the mess hall: Calder says a few words before dinner. Behind P926_TRADS (section 13's P926_NEW).
// Words: SW2 (CS1 checks).
k: 711
title: Twelve weeks aboard
when: arrival +84
at: 17:30-17:55
min: 15
prio: 1
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: 1
who: calder always, torres-zeke always, works 60%, friends-of-host 40%, everyone 15%
anim: talk
host: calder
from: calder

== mail
- Twelve weeks aboard tomorrow. A toast in the mess at {time}, before the Sunday table. Two minutes. Then dinner.

== ask
- Twelve weeks! The Chief's making a toast in the mess before dinner.
- A toast for the new hand later. Calder's giving it. Short, I'd bet.   #funny
- Twelve weeks aboard. That's nearly a whole season.

== here
- To twelve weeks. And the next twelve.   #warm
- Eighty-four days. The Chief counted. Of course she did.   #funny
- Cups up. Calder's about to speak.

== thanks
- Calder raises a cup at the head of the table. "Twelve weeks. Eighty-four days. Still here, still learning. Good." The table drinks to you.   #warm

== chatter
- The Chief toasted the new hand. Twelve weeks. It took nine seconds.   #funny
- Twelve weeks aboard, and a toast from Calder. That's rare.   #warm
